RUN_COMPLETE: cursor-for-gen-z

Today's entry is **Cursor for gen z**, a fake product called **Lowkey**: a code editor where your group chats are the files. You press Tab to accept a suggested reply, a "vibe linter" flags full stops and other signs of sincerity, and an Agent mode gets you out of brunch. It took 2 rerolls because Steam/wolves and Duolingo/dogs were already in the history. Both validation passes (before and after the visual check) came back OK.

- **Design:** a pastel Y2K look on a lilac background, with periwinkle `#5B4BFF`, hot pink `#FF3FA4`, glossy chrome bubbles and Syne / Space Grotesk / Space Mono fonts. None of the last 7 entries uses this style, palette or font set.
- **Images:** I made 3 testimonial headshots and all passed on the first try. I skipped the hero image (the hero is a big headline over an editor mockup) and demo images (the demo is editor screens, no photo slots).
- **Demo:** you can switch chats, search them, and accept, cycle or reject the suggested reply with Tab, Alt+] and Esc or the on-screen buttons. It also has a model picker, a "rizz temperature" slider that goes off the rails above 1.6, one-click linter fixes, and an Agent window that shows a step-by-step log.
- **Gallery:** rebuilt with 131 entries. The eBay for goats card now shows its longer hero subtitle instead of its one-liner, which matches the other 127 cards. I also fixed the order of the two June 12 entries so it matches the previous order.
- **Visual check:** I took 2 screenshots and made 1 fix. The glossy bubble behind the Pro pricing tier was pushing that card's content down; it now sits behind the content. I didn't take a second screenshot to confirm the fix. One small leftover: the demo's "personality retained" counter starts at 20% instead of 14%, which is cosmetic and I left it.

`state/history.json` and `state/runs/2026-10-22.log` are updated. I didn't run any git commands.
